<title>USA: AMBAC qualifies 16 muni bond issues for insurance.</title>
<headline>AMBAC qualifies 16 muni bond issues for insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>AMBAC Indemnity Corp said Tuesday it qualified for bond insurance the following 16 municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today:</p>
<p>--Alabama Building Finance Agency, $22.545 million bonds, by direct purchase.  </p>
<p>--Auburn, Ala., $11 million general obligation bonds.</p>
<p>--Denver Board of Water, Colo., $16.975 million GO refunding bonds.</p>
<p>--Laurens-Marathon School District, Iowa, $1.7 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Cohasset, Mass., $4.515 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Plymouth, Mich., $7.355 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Laurel, Miss., $4 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Lumberton Twonship, N.J., $4.029 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Los Lunas School District No 1, N.M., $2.5 million GOs.</p>
</text>
